{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1000", "sample_idx": 22, "model_name": "google/gemma-3n-e2b-it", "content": "Raymond III Count of Tripoli was a powerful ruler who reigned as Count of Tripoli from 1146 to 1193. He is considered one of the most significant rulers of the Crusader states and a pivotal figure in the history of the Levant. His reign was marked by military campaigns political maneuvering and significant contributions to the economic and cultural development of Tripoli.\n\n*Early Life and Ascension*\n\nRaymond III was born in 1146 the son of Raymond II Count of Tripoli. He inherited the countship at a young age following his father's death. His early reign saw him consolidating his power and dealing with internal factions within Tripoli. He proved to be a capable administrator successfully managing the region's resources and maintaining order. He fostered strong relationships with neighboring rulers particularly those of the Kingdom of Jerusalem and the Byzantine Empire. He skillfully navigated the complex political landscape of the Crusader states avoiding unnecessary conflicts and securing Tripoli's position as a vital trading hub.\n\n*Military Campaigns and Expansion*\n\nRaymond III’s reign was characterized by numerous military campaigns aimed at expanding Tripoli's territory and influence. He led successful expeditions against the Seljuk Turks and the Ayyubid dynasty securing important coastal regions and establishing new trade routes. He also engaged in conflicts with the Fatimids of Egypt protecting Tripoli’s interests in the Eastern Mediterranean. His military prowess and strategic thinking earned him a reputation as a formidable warrior and a respected leader among his peers. Raymond III's military successes greatly enhanced Tripoli's economic prosperity and solidified its position as a major player in the region. He expanded Tripoli's control over coastal areas and established fortified settlements along the Mediterranean coast.\n\n*Legacy and Reforms*\n\nRaymond III’s reign left a lasting legacy on Tripoli. He is remembered for his administrative reforms his commitment to justice and his promotion of trade and commerce. He fostered a thriving economy attracting merchants and artisans from across the Mediterranean. He also invested in infrastructure building roads and ports to facilitate trade and communication. He was a patron of the arts and culture supporting scholars and artists.  His reign saw a flourishing of intellectual and artistic activity in Tripoli.  Raymond III’s legacy extended beyond his military achievements and political acumen. He is considered a symbol of strength and resilience in the face of adversity and a model of effective leadership. His reign established Tripoli as a powerful and prosperous state contributing significantly to the development of the Crusader states and the broader Mediterranean world.\n\n\n\n", "logprobs": [{"token": "Raymond", "logprob": -0.14342188835144043}, {"token": "▁III", "logprob": -1.6689286894688848e-06}, {"token": "▁Count", "logprob": -4.5060096454108134e-05}, {"token": "▁of", "logprob": -2.50339189733495e-06}, {"token": "▁Tripoli", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": "▁was", "logprob": -0.0798519179224968}, {"token": "▁a", "logprob": -0.04111293703317642}, {"token": "▁powerful", "logprob": -0.5501455068588257}, {"token": "▁ruler", "logprob": -0.6038829684257507}, {"token": "▁who", "logprob": -0.6161623597145081}, {"token": "▁reigned", "logprob": -0.5910662412643433}, {"token": "▁as", "logprob": -0.7818617224693298}, {"token": "▁Count", "logprob": -0.0014425835106521845}, {"token": "▁of", "logprob": -0.0009466695482842624}, {"token": "▁Tripoli", "logprob": -5.61460001335945e-05}, {"token": "▁from", "logprob": -0.001135181519202888}, {"token": "▁", "logprob": -0.0035432910080999136}, {"token": "1", "logprob": -0.00015352977789007127}, {"token": "1", "logprob": -0.001061352901160717}, {"token": "4", "logprob": -0.8260542154312134}, {"token": "6", "logprob": -0.11